---
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
import TopBar from "../../components/TopBar.astro";
import { v, importmap } from "../../lib/v.mjs";
---
<Page
  title="Image Resizer: Resize One or Many Images in Bulk | jsal.io"
  description="Resize and crop one image or hundreds at once to an exact size, free and in your browser. JPG, PNG, WebP and HEIC in; JPG, PNG or WebP out. Nothing is uploaded."
  path="/image-resizer/"
  ogDescription="Resize and crop one image or a whole batch to an exact size, free and in your browser. Nothing is uploaded."
  ogImage="image-resizer"
  ogImageAlt="Image Resizer: resize, crop and convert one image or a whole batch of JPG, PNG, WebP and HEIC"
  icon="/img/icons/image-resizer.svg"
  mono={false}
>
<script is:inline slot="head" type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebApplication",
    "name": "Image Resizer",
    "url": "https://jsal.io/image-resizer/",
    "description": "Resize, crop and convert one image or a whole batch in the browser. Accepts JPG, PNG, WebP and HEIC; saves JPG, PNG or WebP. Nothing is uploaded.",
    "dateModified": "2026-10-30",
    "applicationCategory": "MultimediaApplication",
    "operatingSystem": "Any (web browser)",
    "isAccessibleForFree": true,
    "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD" },
    "author": { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://jsal.io/#john", "name": "John Salvador", "url": "https://jsal.io/" },
    "isPartOf": { "@id": "https://jsal.io/#website" }
  }
  </script>
<link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href={v("styles.css", "/image-resizer/")}>
<script is:inline slot="head" type="importmap" set:html={importmap("/image-resizer/", ["./js/main.js", "./js/state.js", "./js/imaging.js", "./js/export.js", "./js/editor.js", "./js/grid.js", "./js/ui.js", "./js/zip.js", "./js/folder.js", "./vendor/heic-to/heic-to.min.js?v=1.6.6"])}></script>
<script is:inline slot="head" type="module" src={v("js/main.js", "/image-resizer/")}></script>
  <main class="app">

    <!-- Top bar shared by every jsal.io app (styles in /shell.css; the logo menu and theme button come from /nav.js) -->
    <TopBar class="app-header"><h1 slot="title" class="jsal-title"><img class="jsal-title-ico" src={v("/img/icons/image-resizer.svg")} alt="" width="22" height="22">Image <span class="hl">Resizer</span><span class="sr-only">: Resize one or many images in bulk</span></h1>
<a class="jsal-link" href="#about">About</a></TopBar>
    <p class="jsal-for">Resize one image or a whole batch to an exact size, fast. Nothing is uploaded.</p>

    <section class="controls" aria-label="Settings">

      <h2 class="section-label" id="sizeLabel">Output size</h2>

      <!-- To add a preset: copy a seg-btn and set data-size="WIDTHxHEIGHT" -->
      <div class="segment-group" role="group" aria-labelledby="sizeLabel">
        <button class="seg-btn active" data-size="1200x628">
          <span class="seg-label">1200 × 628</span>
          <span class="seg-hint">Blog / social share</span>
        </button>
        <button class="seg-btn" data-size="640x420">
          <span class="seg-label">640 × 420</span>
          <span class="seg-hint">Small feature image</span>
        </button>
        <button class="seg-btn" id="originalBtn" title="Keep each image's own dimensions — no resizing or cropping, just convert the format">
          <span class="seg-label">Original</span>
          <span class="seg-hint">Keep sizes, convert only</span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="custom-row">
        <div class="input-group">
          <label for="cw">W</label>
          <input type="number" id="cw" placeholder="1200" min="32" max="20000" />
        </div>
        <div class="input-sep" aria-hidden="true">×</div>
        <div class="input-group">
          <label for="ch">H</label>
          <input type="number" id="ch" placeholder="628" min="32" max="20000" />
        </div>
        <button class="jsal-btn" id="customResize">Apply</button>
      </div>

      <!-- Recent custom sizes (last 5) — filled by JS -->
      <div id="recentSizes" class="recent-sizes" role="group" aria-label="Recent sizes" hidden></div>

      <!-- Quality maps to encoder quality: 0.7 / 0.85 / 0.92 -->
      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-label" id="qualityLabel">Quality</span>
        <div class="jsal-seg" role="group" aria-labelledby="qualityLabel">
          <button class="quality-btn" data-quality="0.7">Low</button>
          <button class="quality-btn" data-quality="0.85">Med</button>
          <button class="quality-btn active" data-quality="0.92">High</button>
        </div>
        <span class="option-hint" id="qualityHint">Sharp output, larger file size</span>
      </div>

      <div class="option-row">
        <span class="option-label" id="formatLabel">Format</span>
        <div class="jsal-seg" role="group" aria-labelledby="formatLabel">
          <button class="format-btn active" data-format="jpeg">JPG</button>
          <button class="format-btn" data-format="png">PNG</button>
          <button class="format-btn" data-format="webp">WebP</button>
        </div>
        <span class="option-hint" id="formatHint">Smaller file, good for photos</span>
      </div>

      <!-- Shown only once images are loaded (to add more); before that the big preview is the drop target -->
      <div class="divider" data-needs-images></div>

      <h2 class="section-label" data-needs-images>Load images</h2>

      <button id="drop" class="drop-zone" data-needs-images>
        <span class="drop-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3v12"/><path d="m17 8-5-5-5 5"/><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/></svg>
        </span>
        <span class="drop-text">
          <span class="drop-title" data-touch="Choose images">Drop images here</span>
          <span class="drop-sub" data-touch="Tap to browse — JPG, PNG, WebP, HEIC">or click to browse — JPG, PNG, WebP, HEIC</span>
        </span>
      </button>

      <input type="file" id="file" multiple accept="image/*,.heic,.heif" hidden />

      <!-- Shown when images are already loaded and new ones are dropped in -->
      <div class="load-choice" id="loadChoice" role="alert" hidden>
        <span class="load-choice-msg" id="loadChoiceMsg"></span>
        <div class="load-choice-btns">
          <button class="btn-choice btn-choice-replace" id="choiceReplace">Replace</button>
          <button class="btn-choice btn-choice-add" id="choiceAdd">Add</button>
          <button class="btn-choice btn-choice-cancel" id="choiceCancel">Cancel</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <h2 class="section-label">Export</h2>

      <div class="option-row option-row-wide">
        <span class="option-label" id="destLabel">Save to</span>
        <div class="jsal-seg" role="group" aria-labelledby="destLabel">
          <button class="dest-btn active" data-dest="files" title="Each image downloads separately to your browser's download location">Downloads</button>
          <button class="dest-btn" data-dest="zip" title="All images in one .zip file">ZIP</button>
          <button class="dest-btn" data-dest="folder" title="Save straight into a folder you choose (Chrome/Edge)">Folder</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="folder-row" id="folderRow" hidden>
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 20a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-7.9a2 2 0 0 1-1.69-.9L9.6 3.9A2 2 0 0 0 7.93 3H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v13a2 2 0 0 0 2 2Z"/></svg>
        <span class="folder-name" id="folderName">No folder chosen</span>
        <button class="folder-change" id="folderChange">Choose…</button>
      </div>

      <!-- Off by default, so files keep the names they came with; the example is the first image's name as it will save -->
      <label class="name-tick">
        <input type="checkbox" id="sizeInName" aria-labelledby="sizeInNameLabel" aria-describedby="nameEg">
        <span><span class="name-tick-label" id="sizeInNameLabel">Add the size to file names</span><span class="name-eg" id="nameEg">photo-1200x628.jpg</span></span>
      </label>

      <div class="toolbar">
        <button class="jsal-btn primary" id="download" disabled>
          <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 15V3"/><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/><path d="m7 10 5 5 5-5"/></svg>
          <span id="downloadLabel">Download all</span>
        </button>
        <kbd class="toolbar-hint" id="kbdHint"></kbd>
        <button class="jsal-btn danger" id="clear">
          <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 11v6"/><path d="M14 11v6"/><path d="M19 6v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6"/><path d="M3 6h18"/><path d="M8 6V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h4a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v2"/></svg>
          Clear
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="status-bar" id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden>
        <span class="status-dot" id="statusDot"></span>
        <span id="statusText"></span>
      </div>

    </section>

    <section class="workspace" aria-label="Preview">

      <div class="canvas-wrap">
        <!-- Before any images are loaded, the whole preview is a drop target / browse button -->
        <button class="canvas-empty" id="canvasEmpty">
          <span class="canvas-empty-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3v12"/><path d="m17 8-5-5-5 5"/><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/></svg>
          </span>
          <span class="canvas-empty-title" data-touch="Choose images">Drop images here</span>
          <span class="canvas-empty-sub" data-touch="Tap to browse — JPG, PNG, WebP, HEIC">or click to browse — JPG, PNG, WebP, HEIC</span>
        </button>
        <canvas id="out" tabindex="0" aria-label="Crop preview — use arrow keys to reposition the crop"></canvas>
        <div class="canvas-badge" id="canvasBadge"></div>
      </div>
      <p class="crop-hint" id="cropHint"></p>
      <!-- In place of the crop hint when the image is smaller than the output size (editor.js) -->
      <p class="upscale-note" id="upscaleNote" hidden></p>

      <div class="grid-header" id="gridHeader" hidden>
        <h2 class="grid-title">Loaded images</h2>
        <span class="grid-hint" data-touch="Tap to edit crop · Save downloads · Rename files">Click to edit crop · Save downloads · Rename files</span>
      </div>

      <div id="previewGrid" class="preview-grid"></div>

    </section>

  </main>

  <Fragment set:html={`<!-- About: below the app (which fills the first screen); styles in /shell.css -->`} />
  <section class="jsal-about" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-h">
    <h2 id="about-h">About the Image Resizer</h2>
    <p class="jsal-lead">Exact sizes for one image or a batch, with a crop you control, and nothing ever leaves your device.</p>

    <h3>How to use it</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Pick an output size: <strong>1200 × 628</strong> (blog posts and social share images), <strong>640 × 420</strong> (smaller feature images), <strong>Original</strong> to keep each image's size, or type your own width and height.</li>
      <li data-touch="Tap Choose images to pick them from your photos or files.">Drop your images on the page, or click to browse.</li>
      <li>Check the crop. <span data-touch="Tap any image in the strip to edit it, then drag the crop box to choose which part is kept.">Click any image in the strip to edit it, then drag the crop box (or use the arrow keys) to choose which part is kept.</span></li>
      <li>Choose quality and format, then <strong>Download all</strong><span data-touch=""> (<kbd class="mod-key">Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>D</kbd>)</span>. You can also save single images, rename files first, or add the size to every file name (<code>photo-1200x628.jpg</code>).</li>
    </ol>

    <details>
      <summary><h3>What it supports</h3></summary>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Input:</strong> JPG, PNG, WebP and HEIC (iPhone photos).</li>
        <li><strong>Output:</strong> JPG or WebP at low, medium or high quality, or PNG (lossless, keeps transparency, biggest files). Safari can't save WebP, so there it saves JPG.</li>
        <li><strong>Sizes:</strong> presets, any custom size from 32 to 20,000 pixels (your last five are kept as shortcuts), or original size.</li>
        <li><strong>Saving:</strong> one download per image, a single ZIP file, or straight into a folder you choose (Chrome and Edge).</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <h3>Common questions</h3>
    <dl>
      <dt>Is it free?</dt>
      <dd>Yes. There's no sign-up, no watermark and no limit on how many images you resize.</dd>
      <dt>Does it work on a phone?</dt>
      <dd>Yes, in any up-to-date browser on iPhone or Android. Pick images from your photos or files; they save as downloads or a ZIP.</dd>
    </dl>

    <p class="jsal-feedback">Useful? Ideas or problems? <a href="mailto:dev@jsal.io?subject=Image%20Resizer">Email me</a>.</p>
    <p><svg class="jsal-mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect class="jsal-mark-tile" x=".5" y=".5" width="31" height="31" rx="6.5"/><path class="jsal-mark-j" d="M20 15V20a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-9 0"/><path class="jsal-mark-gem" d="M20 5l3 3-3 3-3-3z"/></svg>Made by <a href="/">John Salvador</a>. Also try <a href="/formatter/">Clean Paste</a> for turning Word and Google Docs content into clean HTML, or <a href="/cms-picker/">CMS Picker</a> to compare what each CMS can do. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Page>
